WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.567
21 year

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:01.935
old suspected Pentagon

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.603
leaker, Jack Teixeira

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.671
was back in court

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.006
to waive his right

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.741
to a preliminary hearing.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:09.175
Meanwhile, inside the Pentagon,

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.176
the Air Force unit

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.044
where he was assigned

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.312
has now been stripped

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.080
of the intelligence duties

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.483
it had as an internal probe ramps up.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.250
A short time

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.785
from now, all members of the House

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.320
and Senate will be briefed

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.522
on the extent of the classified leak.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.424
And it reportedly has yielded

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:27.394
another alarming detail about China.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.528
According to The Washington

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:29.729
Post, one Pentagon

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:30.463
assessment shows

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.232
Beijing is about to unveil

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.367
a high tech spy drone unit.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.102
Have a look at that right there.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.371
That would give it surveillance program

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.340
potentially a significant boost

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.274
CNN's Oren Liebermann,

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.876
he's at the Pentagon organ.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:43.710
Oren, as we know,

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.511
the Pentagon

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:45.745
still trying to come to terms

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.380
with the extent of this on a whole host

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.948
of national security threats.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.984
Tell us what specifically we're learning

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.085
about this spy drone.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:54.754
Jim, we have seen

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.556
this supersonic spy drone before.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.957
And the image we just saw right

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.526
there, the double U.S.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.527
spy drone

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.796
that picture from back in 2019

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.831
when China showed it off at a parade.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:05.899
But at the time, it wasn't

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.200
believed to be operational.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.436
It was a sort of prototype or a mockup.

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.371
But according to The Washington Post

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.639
in these leaked documents

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:13.239
we're seeing come

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.741
from the Pentagon documents

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.009
that CNN has not been able

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.744
to obtain or verified.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.846
That program has come a long way

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:22.482
There's WS eight surveillance spy drone,

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:23.683
part of what the U.S.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:24.350
believes is

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.686
part of a Chinese surveillance drone unit

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.822
that's based inland from Shanghai.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.623
Take a look at the capable cities

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.558
of this drone.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.025
It travels

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:33.493
it mock three plus

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:34.527
or more than three times

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.528
the speed of sound

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.431
at an altitude of 100,000 feet so far

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.500
higher than commercial aircraft.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.535
And because of that, because of its speed

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.536
and its altitude,

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.606
it's difficult to detect or to intercept.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.142
Making it another potential addition

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.144
to what we've seen in terms of China's

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:52.245
spy capabilities.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:52.912
And of course,

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:53.346
nobody here

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.981
forgets the Chinese spy balloon

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:55.648
that traveled over

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.016
much of the United States.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.852
What's interesting here is the U.S.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:01:59.486
has seen this

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:01.621
in a bit of a role reversal, if you will.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:02.956
The US had its own

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.958
super supersonic spy drone

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.260
back in the sixties that called the D.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:07.794
21.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.696
It was specifically to spy over China

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:12.365
it conducted four unsuccessful missions

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.767
back in the late sixties, early seventies

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.102
timeframe before that program

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:16.870
was canceled.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.071
Jim, it looks like the Chinese

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.539
have very different intentions

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:21.207
and much broader intentions,

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.442
which would allow them to spy

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.043
on, for example, Taiwan

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.578
and parts of South Korea.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.046
Yeah, frankly,

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.047
those two planes look a lot

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.249
alike, interestingly.

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:29.582
All right.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.050
The fact that the sheriff's unit

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.619
now has been removed,

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:33.453
at least temporarily,

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.255
from its intelligence duties.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:37.223
Is that a standard step

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.191
when the Pentagon's

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.959
doing a damage assessment

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:40.960
here, in effect,

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.395
to have that unit removed,

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:43.796
or does it signal

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:44.964
that this is worse than we knew?

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.234
Well, it
certainly signals that the Air Force

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.170
is taking this very seriously.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.237
Secretary of the Air Force,

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.105
Frank Kendall,

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.574
removing the 102nd intelligence wing's

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:55.508
mission from them.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:56.342
They will no longer

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.344
at least temporarily collect

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.512
and put together data

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:00.580
for combatant commanders

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.081
and other senior leaders.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.249
Other wings will do that

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.551
as the Air Force investigates

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.653
other steps the Air Force is taking.

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:07.620
Take a look at this list

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.022
within the next 30 days.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.757
All of the Air Force will do a stand down

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:11.858
or essentially a review

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:12.992
of security procedures

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.827
and how to handle classified documents.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:15.862
They'll also reassess

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.130
security procedures

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.765
around classified documents

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.967
in the handling of sensitive information.

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.835
Finally, everyone who has access to

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.103
this will be validated

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.738
for their need to know basis. Jim.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:27.740
Oren Liebermann

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.175
good to have you at the Pentagon.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.710
As I mentioned a short time ago,

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:31.978
every member of Congress

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.479
will be briefed on the Pentagon

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.547
leak this afternoon.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.649
CNN's Manu Raju is on Capitol Hill.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:37.517
Manu, of course,

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:38.585
So this is not the committee

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:39.252
that is cleared

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.386
for this level of intelligence,

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:41.020
a bit broader,

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.089
probably a bit more of a general

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.190
briefing on the extent.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:44.791
But but what are you

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.326
hearing from lawmakers

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:48.494
in advance of this briefing?

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.862
Well, there is a lot of concern,

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:50.430
and they do

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:51.931
want to learn more information

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.733
from senior administration officials

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.500
led by the director

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.536
of National Intelligence, Avril Haines,

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:58.371
who will be in the Senate this afternoon

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.572
and then in the House

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:00.373
with a number of other

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:01.708
national security officials

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.343
detailing the extent of this leak

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:05.645
and how exactly a 21 year old

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.247
air national airman

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.281
from the Massachusetts

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.282
Air National Guard

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:11.551
had access to classified information.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.052
And in talking to

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.053
senior members

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:14.887
in both parties,

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.356
there is ample concern

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:18.291
about how he got this information

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:19.392
and what Congress should do

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:20.994
to prevent this from happening again.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:27.533
To me, the

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.669
classification of the documents

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:30.370
ought to be reserved

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.372
for the very most

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:34.540
exceptional national security risks,

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.375
and not

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:36.943
as broadly as it is now,

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:37.744
but as we've seen

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:39.412
with classified materials.

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:42.015
Being at President Trump's

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:44.917
home to President Pence's

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.620
office and at President Biden's residence

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.590
there, people are not taking care

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.425
of classified materials

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:53.626
the way they should

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.561
And how in the heck with there

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:59.499
not some system in place

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.134
that said,

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.268
if this guy was copying

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:04.437
this many documents

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.205
why wasn't there a lot going on,

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:06.673
especially with

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:08.908
the security classification?

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.810
And that second senator there was Senator

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.211
Mark Warner, who chairs the Senate

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.313
Intelligence Committee,

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.280
who also indicated

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.315
that he is still pushing

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:16.683
to get all the access

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:17.817
to the classified records

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.452
that were at the homes of Joe

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.888
Biden and Donald Trump and Mike Pence.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:22.722
He's expecting

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:24.223
another tranche of documents

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.392
as soon as today as Congress

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.493
grapples with this issue.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.529
Why all these classified documents

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:30.363
appear to be leaking,

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:31.531
appear to be in the wrong places,

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:33.900
including this major leak that happened

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.436
and deciding what they need to do next.

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:37.303
And Senator Warner asked

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:38.137
such a key question there,

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:39.772
which is why no tracking of this,

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.607
because the guy was printing it,

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.042
print it out and then sharing it.

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.310
Manu Raju on the Hill.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.678
Thanks so much, Boris.

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:46.012
Yeah,

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:47.647
one of many unanswered questions

00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:48.948
at this point, Jim.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.183
Let's dig deeper

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:52.251
now on the case against Jack to share

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:53.353
with Bradley Moss.

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:53.953
He's an attorney

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.955
who specializes in litigation

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:57.390
related to national security

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.991
and security clearance law.

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.193
He's also a law partner

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:01.794
at the offices of Mark

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:03.062
Zaid, Bradley,

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.063
thank you so much for taking time

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:05.698
to chat with us today.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:06.899
So there was a delay,

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.701
the defense asking for the trial

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.136
to be set back about two weeks.

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:12.972
The prosecution supporting that decision.

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:14.640
Did that surprise you?

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:15.341
Not really.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:15.975
You know, look,

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:17.543
there's only so much to do right now

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:18.544
at the beginning for this.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.880
This would've
been a very preliminary hearing.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.280
If anything,

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.348
we've been talking about bail,

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:23.950
which I don't see happening.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.284
He has got a public defender.

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:26.886
What they are most likely doing.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:28.354
Given the evidence we've seen both

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:29.021
in the indictment

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:30.156
and the media reporting,

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:31.858
they're likely talking about a plea deal

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:32.592
they're trying to see

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:34.127
if there's a viable path

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:35.528
to negotiate something

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:37.163
by which this guy gets maybe

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:39.399
ten to 12 years in prison, outlines

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:40.800
the entirety of what he did

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:41.367
to the government

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:42.902
from a intelligence standpoint,

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.070
can make sure to close up

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.805
any gaps in its systems

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:47.407
and that he can go forward with his life

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:48.508
once he gets out,

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:49.275
because it's

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:50.309
hard to imagine

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:52.445
what a defense might look like. Right.

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:54.247
Because the evidence there,

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:56.616
there's a clear trail back to him.

00:06:56.616 --> 00:06:57.116
Yes.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.017
The evidence mean

00:06:58.017 --> 00:06:59.185
the defense is simply going

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:00.253
to be poking holes

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.053
in the government's case

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:02.221
if this went to trial,

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.122
because it would be the government's

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:04.223
burden, obviously,

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:06.225
to demonstrate beyond a reasonable doubt

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:06.626
that he had,

00:07:06.626 --> 00:07:07.393
in fact, done this,

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:08.694
that he had the access,

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:10.163
that he took the documents

00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:11.631
that he posted it on this court.

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:13.099
They likely could do so,

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:13.699
but it would be

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:14.767
a little complicated for them

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.335
because there'd be issues of classified

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:17.103
access.

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:18.871
There's classified as a statute

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:19.939
called the classified information

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:20.773
Procedures Act

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:22.074
that would come into play,

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.277
any number of complicating factors.

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:24.911
So if the government

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:26.245
can play this out with him

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:27.346
and they get what they need

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:29.382
from purposes of a punishment standpoint,

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:30.383
they'll be happy with that.

00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:31.584
Now, National Security

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:32.852
Council spokesperson

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:35.121
John Kirby was here in CNN News

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:35.755
Central yesterday,

00:07:35.755 --> 00:07:36.622
and he spoke with my colleague,

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:37.290
Jim Sciutto.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:37.957
He acknowledged

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:40.259
that some of the classified documents

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:41.828
appear to have been

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:42.728
manipulated

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:44.430
and that some of them had information

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.631
that was false.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:46.399
Could that lessen

00:07:46.399 --> 00:07:48.067
the severity of the charges

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:49.469
that to share his facing?

00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:50.736
It won't lessen the severity,

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:52.071
but it's a reason for him

00:07:52.071 --> 00:07:53.773
to look into a plea deal,

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:54.740
because if he can

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.709
then debrief the government

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:58.911
on all the documents he knows he took.

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.613
And they can start to track down

00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:01.848
which ones were authentic

00:08:01.848 --> 00:08:02.515
that are out there

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:04.283
that are being viewed all over the media

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:05.885
and which ones were manipulated.

00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:07.253
They can clarify for their own

00:08:07.253 --> 00:08:08.187
damage assessment

00:08:08.187 --> 00:08:09.922
what actually got leaked out.

00:08:09.922 --> 00:08:11.357
Where did we have holes

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:12.992
in our security protocols?

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:14.494
And what is the extent of the damage

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:15.695
to US national security?

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:16.762
I'm curious about something

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:19.065
that Oren talked about, and that is that

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:20.166
his unit

00:08:20.166 --> 00:08:21.467
was essentially stripped

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:23.236
of its intelligence mission.

00:08:23.236 --> 00:08:24.370
Does that imply to you

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.272
that other people may be facing

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:27.173
potential charges,

00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:29.675
perhaps supervisors in an oversight role

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:31.711
that kind of let them get away with this?

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:32.545
Well, I think at a minimum,

00:08:32.545 --> 00:08:33.613
that was a required,

00:08:33.613 --> 00:08:34.747
you know, short term thing.

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:36.249
You had this massive breach,

00:08:36.249 --> 00:08:37.750
huge breakdown of security protocols.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.185
They had to stop at every there

00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:40.119
everything there

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:41.988
to start doing an initial review,

00:08:41.988 --> 00:08:43.990
whether or not security messed up,

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:46.359
why he was able to hand transcribe

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:48.594
some of this stuff. And no one noticed.

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:49.795
That's at a minimum

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:51.063
going to possibly result

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:52.431
in personnel actions.

00:08:52.431 --> 00:08:53.099
I don't necessarily know

00:08:53.099 --> 00:08:53.900
about criminal charges,

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:55.501
but they've got to do a review for that.

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:56.102
Yeah.

00:08:56.102 --> 00:08:57.703
A story we will continue to watch.

00:08:57.703 --> 00:08:58.804
Bradley, thank you so much for sharing

00:08:58.804 --> 00:08:59.939
your story any time.

